            "en": "“पित्राज्ञा,” you say, “a father's command,” and the mirror in the statue's hand clears. In it the travellers are reflected, and behind them, in the glass, a long procession of other people, walking up the hill to the throne for a thousand years, each saying a word of welcome. “स्वागतम्,” the statue says. “Welcome.”",
